I replaced the two separate byte copies of `type` and `isFieldExpanded` with a single `std::memcpy` of the adjacent bytes, reducing the copy to one load/store pair. This is faster because it merges the two scalar stores into a single 2-byte move.

```include
#include <cstring>
```

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field)
    , profile(field.profile)
    , profileIndex(field.profileIndex)
{
    std::memcpy(&type, &field.type, sizeof(type) + sizeof(isFieldExpanded));
}
```